Creative-Writing-Rubrics: licensing scope

This repository contains separately licensed components. This index does not
withdraw any earlier grant or relicense third-party material.

HBQ-RS itself remains licensed under Apache License 2.0:
  licenses/Apache-2.0.txt
This includes docs/HBQ_RS_STANDARD.md, schema/, src/, scripts/, tools/, tests/,
implementation examples, prompts/judge/, and generic protocol documentation.

New original CWR expression first offered under this licensing transition uses:
  licenses/CWR-Community-1.0.txt
  LicenseRef-CWR-Community-1.0
The designated application-content paths are registry/, bundles/,
prompts/review/, docs/RUBRIC_BOOK.md, docs/RESEARCH_SYNTHESIS.md, docs/apps.md,
docs/benchmarking.md, docs/synthetic-data.md, and docs/training.md.
The free license permits commercial use and resale by eligible users.
Company Groups with at least US $10,000,000 consolidated annual gross revenue
require separately negotiated permission for that Covered Material.

Original project material outside the designated application-content paths
continues under Apache 2.0 unless it carries a separate explicit license.
No filename or directory designation overrides an earlier or third-party grant.

Material previously offered under Apache 2.0 remains available under that grant,
including material present through commit
8cda421aae3bfbb82a5ca3c4a3d3a5a553f534e8 and earlier releases. New protectable
expression may carry the community condition; changing this index does not
impose it retroactively. Frozen research inputs, historical evidence packages,
quoted works, sources, datasets, and dependencies retain their existing terms.

See docs/LICENSING.md and NOTICE for the scope and prior-grant limitations.
